  "notes": "AtomicChat's uncensored Inkling-2-Mini: a rank-1 LoRA (refusal direction removed per layer, all 24 layers + embedding) baked into their AD-Q4_K (their numbers: 0 refusals on the harmful test sets, MMLU 79.15 vs 80.65). Files in the merged llama.cpp layout (arch inkling2_loop, PR #32694), so it needs kernel bin-inklingm = llama.cpp master e50c254a (2026-11-21); it does not load on bin-inkling. Same runtime rules as inkling-2-mini: A4500 alone (split over both cards ~9 tok/s), compute buffer grows with context x ubatch, reasoning_effort minimal as the server default in the -min configs. ts = A4500,V100. The v100-* configs run AD-IQ3_S (13.3 GB) on the Tesla V100 alone (config gpu: V100, the A4500 stays free for a second server, e.g. start.bat <model> v100 8900). Q4_K split with most layers on the V100 (ts over the 48 looped layer slots, A4500 first): 2/46 and 3/45 run the V100 out of memory, 4/44 18.2 tok/s (A4500 4.9 GB, V100 15.6 GB), 5/43 14.9, 6/42 12.7, 8/40 9.8, 12/36 9.7: every split is about half the speed of one card or worse.",
